 # --- G52 (wave 5.2 gas, 2026-10-28): labels [930]-[945] ---
 # Two gas mechanisms that must change no answer, to the wei. M10 (`Solver._firstStage`): the
 # first stage of a bridge route, tIn -> bs[i], is built once per solve, kept in the pair's
 # `_candsOf` entry keyed on its input, budget and mode, and every later topology opening on bs[i]
 # reads a copy of it (rank and held flag included). M11 (`Math._byRate`): a hop orders its live
 # rates once, and the plain median and every weighted median walk that one order. Each test
 # compares the Solver with the Solver of 653b1dc (test/ref/SolverRef653.sol, frozen with its own
 # Math) on the same state: the same success and the same returndata bytes.
 # Equivalent, written in reports/plano-1026/onda5/G52-gas.md: [932] [934] [938] [942] [946].
 # hops2 (2026-11-06): M10 is gone with the three-hop topologies. With two hops no topology of the
 # main loop shares a pair with another, so the kept first stage was read by none; its eight entries
 # ([930] [931] [935] [936] [937] [939] [940] [941]) are retired with the code they mutated, and the
 # G52 tests that named them are rewritten against the two-hop Solver with successors of their own.
