  # TickMath certificate (test/TickMathCertificate.t.sol, docs/assurance/tickmath-certificate.tsv). Each
  # constant is moved to its other rounding of 2^128/sqrt(1.0001)^(2^i); bits 2, 4 and 12 move no output on
  # any of the 1,774,545 ticks, so only the source line can show them. Product truncations whose rounding up
  # moves no output (bits 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11, 12 and 13, measured), the inversion's floor, the ceil
  # mask and `sgt(tick, 0)` -> `iszero(slt(tick, 0))` (tick 0 inverts to 2^128 - 1, which rounds up to the
  # same 2^96) are equivalent mutants and are not listed; so are dropping `unchecked` (no step wraps, see
  # the bounds of tickmath_certificate.py) and dropping the signextend, the identity on a clean int24.
